 itself, and neither line wrong on its own. That is what a text merge produces when one side EDITS a recipe line and the other RE-ADDS the version it replaced, and no author sees it because each is reading their own diff. THE WIRED-TWICE POPULATION IS A MEASURED ZERO, so its refusal is never a backlog: it is a one-line deletion whose author is still in the room, which is exactly the property the coverage arms lack. Whether a check belongs in the recipe or at handoff is decided by measuring its backlog first, never by how important the check feels -- equivalently (hq_U, adopted by the ceo as CEO-520): a live-tree arm is legitimate exactly when its red population is small enough that EVERY red has a named author still in the room. ⛔ THE MEASURED ZERO IS THE PRECONDITION AND NOT A PLEASANT FACT ABOUT TODAY: if this count is ever nonzero AT REST, ARM 7 moves to handoff_status.sh, because a standing red left in a recipe trains every reader to skip the arm. ⭐ And the zero is trustworthy only because the arm walks the recursive make into test-postoffice: a count that stopped at the target boundary would report the same zero with a cross-target double in plain sight, resting the precondition on the instrument's blind spot instead of on the tree.
